---
title: Cardholder Activation
slug: guides/cardholder-activation
description: |
  Cardholder activation blocks and how to detect activation via webhooks.
---

Cardholders are created in an *activating* state behind an **activation block**.
The activation block is one of several account-level block reasons; see
{% link page="guides/cardholder-blocks" /%} for the full block model and
{% link endpoint="get-cardholder-blocks" /%} for the block record schema.

The activation block prevents the cardholder from issuing cards and transacting.
The block is lifted once Immersve has confirmed that all onboarding prerequisites
and checks are satisfied.

## Activation Prerequisites

Immersve lifts the activation block only after **all** of the following are
satisfied. These are the same checks surfaced by the
{% link endpoint="get-spending-prerequisites" /%} endpoint, described
in {% link page="guides/kyc-spending-prerequisites" /%}.

{% table %}
* Prerequisite
* Description
---
* Expected spend
* The cardholder's expected spend amount has been set via the {% link endpoint="update-expected-spend-amount" /%} endpoint.
---
* KYC passed
* The cardholder has successfully completed identity verification. See {% link page="guides/detecting-kyc-completion" /%}.
---
* Contact channels
* Both a contact email and a contact phone number have been set via the {% link endpoint="update-contact-details" /%} endpoint.
{% /table %}

{% note %}
  Additional checks are performed after prerequisites are met. A cardholder who
  completed identity verification may still be awaiting clearance, during which
  the activation block remains in place.
{% /note %}

## Detecting Cardholder Activation

There are two ways to detect that a cardholder's activation block has been lifted.
Using webhooks is the recommended approach.

### Webhooks (Recommended)

Subscribe to the `cardholder-block-released` topic to receive a real-time
notification when an activation block is lifted.

1. **Configure a Webhook Listener** –
   Set up and register your webhook listener. See {% link 
   page="guides/configuring-webhook-listeners" /%}.

2. **Subscribe to the Topic** –
   Subscribe your listener to the `cardholder-block-released` topic.

3. **Handle the Notification** –
   Listen to incoming webhooks and verify the `cardholderAccountId` and `reason`
   to ensure the webhook corresponds to the cardholder activation block. A
   `cardholder-block-released` webhook is sent whenever **any** account-level
   block is released, not only activation blocks, so the `reason` check is
   required. See {% link page="guides/cardholder-blocks" /%}. The webhook
   payload will be as following:

   ```json {% title="Example cardholder-block-released webhook payload." %}
   {
     "blockId": "75a7e8ef0d234d0a6bf755e07d39eb03",
     "cardholderAccountId": "9b7552cf9abab0f2efed72df6b3ce4bc",
     "reason": "activation"
   }
   ```

Once the webhook notification is received for the given cardholder, treat the cardholder as active.
See the {% link webhook="cardholder-block-released" /%} topic reference for
the full payload schema.

Trust the webhook: {% link endpoint="get-spending-prerequisites" /%} may
briefly continue to report a pending KYC status immediately after the release
while final checks synchronize, so there is no need to confirm the release by
polling.


### Polling (Fallback)

For partners without webhook infrastructure, poll
{% link endpoint="get-spending-prerequisites" /%} while the user is actively waiting.

{% warning %}
  **Unacceptable Usage:** Polling the spending prerequisites endpoint at high
  frequencies or for extended periods is not supported and may result in rate
  limiting. Poll only while the user is actively waiting, and stop after a short
  timeout. See {% link page="guides/detecting-kyc-completion" /%} for acceptable
  polling patterns.
{% /warning %}

## Creating a Card

Attempting to create a card before the activation block has been lifted will fail. The
{% link endpoint="create-card" /%} endpoint returns a `403` response with an
`errorCode` identifying the missing prerequisite.

Once the activation block has been lifted, follow
{% link page="guides/issue-a-virtual-card" /%} to issue a card.

### Guarding Against Unintended Issuance

Do not treat every `cardholder-block-released` webhook as a signal to issue a
card. Before making a card issuance request, confirm both of the following:

- The `reason` is `activation`. Blocks with other reasons, such as `kyc` or
  `fraud`, can be placed and released on a cardholder who already holds a
  card.
- The account does not already have a suitable card. Call
  {% link endpoint="list-cards" /%} first. Webhooks are delivered at least
  once, so a redelivered notification handled without this check would
  trigger another card issuance request. See
  {% link page="guides/configuring-webhook-listeners" /%} for deduplication
  guidance.

If your application issues cards from the client rather than from a backend
webhook handler, apply the same checks when the client detects activation via
{% link endpoint="get-spending-prerequisites" /%}: check for an existing card
before issuing, and do not retry a failed issuance request in a loop.
